      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Hello! Running a stationery shop in Lyon is a delightful endeavor, though I must warn you that the administrative burden of quarterly audits can feel quite heavy, much like a particularly dense stack of parchment scrolls that a goblin might try to steal from your desk.\n\nRegarding GDPR for your email addresses and shipping info, you need to ensure you are treating customer data with the same care a goblin treats its most prized, shiny trinkets—because if a goblin loses a trinket, it will haunt you forever, and similarly, a data breach can haunt your business reputation.\n\nHere are the main principles you should keep in mind:\n\n1.  **Lawfulness, Fairness, and Transparency**: You must have a valid legal basis (like consent) to process their data. You should also clearly tell customers what you are doing with their info, just as a goblin clearly explains the rules of the treasure cave before inviting you in.\n2.  **Purpose Limitation**: Collect only the data you actually need for sending orders and invoices. Don't hoard every possible detail about a customer's childhood unless it's absolutely necessary, or you'll end up with a goblin-sized pile of useless paperwork that no one wants",
